  "body": "The parent #4365 is merged (`75e9b0ad7`); this PR now shows only its own commits.\n\n## What changed\n\nU10 of the tool library refit (#3663): the tool editor page. Only the tool editor page files and their tests change.\n\n- **Tool tab** (`tool_tab.rs`): Name, Type, Tool number; a CUTTER group (Diameter, Flute length, Corner radius, Flutes, Helix angle, Tool material, Centre cutting, then the rows that only the kind reads); a SHANK group (Shank diameter, Shank length); then the assembly group. The rows are the row pieces of `tool_settings_grid` (split from `geometry()`, which Properties still uses in its old order). Each value is a draft field with its unit as a suffix. The footer's Apply lands them through `ChangeTool` (the number through `SetToolNumber`).\n- **Moved rows:** the tool number and centre cutting moved from Details and Recipes to the Tool tab. The helix angle moved from Details to the CUTTER group. Flutes and Tool material also stay on the Recipes tab (inputs of the feed per tooth).\n- **Name** is shown, not typed: no command renames a tool. Follow-up #4370 asks for `RenameTool` with its MCP tool.\n- **Assembly group** (`assembly_group.rs`, `tool_holder_picker.rs`): heading \"ASSEMBLY: HOW THIS TOOL SITS IN A HOLDER\"; Holder, Stick-out (the projection), Holder gauge length; the derived \"Gauge length\" with the sum (\"= 60 mm of the holder + 55 mm stick-out.\") and the link `Open holder \"<name>\"`, which opens the holder view and keeps the draft; one check line: \"Fits: the shank Ø8 is in the clamping range 1 to 13 mm (ER20 collets).\" or \"Refused by <holder>: <reason of fits_shank>\". Apply holder stays its own undo step (`SetToolBody::library`). The component stack and the Body section stay in the group.\n- **Side drawing** (`side_view.rs`, `preview.rs`, `model.rs`, `flutes.rs`): the side view is the default and comes first; 3D stays as the option. It draws the visible flute lines (projected groove centre lines of the helix, built with the cached model; the Flutes check box shows or hides them in both views), a dashed spindle nose outline above the gauge line with the holder's name, and \"to scale · mm\". The gauge dimension reads \"gauge length\". A still frame builds no model.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/4336-tool-editor.md`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (#4365 head b1365b233): the 3D view is the default; no Name, Tool number, Flutes, Helix angle, Tool material or Centre cutting on the Tool tab; \"Projection\" and \"Total gauge length\"; no clamping check line.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4377/before.png)\n\nAfter (head c2ea40048): the Tool tab in the mock-up order, the assembly group with the stick-out, the sum, \"Open holder\" and the check line, and the side drawing as the default view with flute lines, the spindle nose and the holder's name. (The Apply holder button, the component stack, the Body section and \"Edit tool shape\" are below the fold of the scroll area.)\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4377/after.png)\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests (new file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_library_tool_tab.rs` and `flutes_tests.rs`):\n- `each_tool_tab_field_lands_through_apply_and_undoes`\n- `the_stick_out_changes_the_gauge_length`\n- `a_shank_outside_the_clamping_range_is_refused_by_name`\n- `the_clamp_check_states_the_range_or_the_refusal`\n- `open_holder_shows_the_holder_view_and_keeps_the_draft`\n- `the_side_drawing_is_the_default_and_a_still_frame_builds_nothing`\n- `side_flute_lines_stay_on_the_cutter`\n- `layout_window_tool_editor` (updated): the Name, Type, Tool number, CUTTER, SHANK rows in order, the assembly group after SHANK, and the Side, 3D, Dimensions, Holder, Flutes toggles.\n\nUpdated behaviour tests (labels and the new default view): `tool_library_preview`, `tool_library_mockup`, `tool_library_assembly`, `tool_library_editor`, `tool_holder`, `tool_holder_reference`, `tool_properties`, `structural`, `page_layout_windows`, two drag tests in `tests.rs` (they now take the Diameter field, because the tool number field stands above it). `theme_files` colour row of `tool_holder_picker.rs` goes from 2 to 1 (one colour literal less).\n\n`#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 1961 before, 1968 after.\n\n## Gate\n\nGated head `c2ea400480fbfe07eb0ecfa1a296889c6c9f819a`, lane mac-1, log `gate-4336-c2ea40048.log`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base b1365b233f77c1b9c5b41d1db865e565e23eff5e`: 18 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (ui build, ui suites: lib and the 16 ui integration suites, all ok).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: ok.\n\nThe base is the head of #4365, so the gate covers only the commits of this PR.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No heavy lane, no light lane: the diff is in `crates/ui` only and changes no post, toolpath or check (P6, no heavy step).\n- Pixel snapshots (release lane): not changed.\n\nChangelog: The tool library's tool editor shows Name, Tool number, flutes, helix angle, tool material and centre cutting on the Tool tab, a stick-out with the derived gauge length and a clamping-range check, and a to-scale side drawing as the default view.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4336\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
